  "text": "Recipe: Peas Potato Masala\nCreator: Alpesh Parmar\nCategory: Pita Pocket\nIngredients: potatoes, green peas, red onion, green chili, mustard seeds, cumin seeds, turmeric powder, red chilli powder, lemon juice, amchur powder, salt, Ezekiel 4:9 bread\nCooking methods: boil, saute, grill\nInstructions: Boil potatoes and peas. Mash them slightly.\nHeat a pan. Dry sauté mustard seeds and cumin seeds.\nAdd green chilies and turmeric powder. Add mashed potato and peas too. Add salt (if using) and lemon juice.\nCook for a few minutes. Turn off the flame and set aside.\nMake a sandwich with Peas Potato Masala between two slices of Ezekiel 4:9 bread. Grill both sides in a sandwich maker or a non-stick griddle till golden.\nNotes: A recipe with BEANS (green peas), TUBERS (potatoes), RAINBOW VEGGIES (red onion, green chili), LIME-LEMON-VINEGAR (lemon juice), HERBS & SPICES (various).\nEzekiel Sandwich with Peas Potato Masala",
